From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:03:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: Invalidate the ISP when the sensor information
 is missing

Without the sensor information the IPA is not initialised, but the
software ISP still reported itself valid. The simple pipeline then
waits forever for metadata on every request, which stalls cameras that
bypass the ISP, such as YUV sensors.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp
index 28e2a36..fc66222 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/software_isp.cpp
@@ -137,6 +137,7 @@ SoftwareIsp::SoftwareIsp(PipelineHandler *pipe, const CameraSensor *sensor,
 	int ret = sensor->sensorInfo(&sensorInfo);
 	if (ret) {
 		LOG(SoftwareIsp, Error) << "Camera sensor information not available";
+		debayer_.reset();
 		return;
 	}
 
